I re-queued the fix for #918 with the manager as commit `f3aef5e6`. Nothing is merged yet; the manager posts its verdict on the issue.

- **Why re-queue:** the last red result was not caused by the change. The manager's pipeline 3097093702 was cancelled before it started, so no gate ran. The earlier red was a lost build runner, and Jody said to re-queue unchanged.
- **The fix:** it is the same change as the earlier attempts (80265c43 and 682b4959). Black's deadline is now 5 minutes plus 5 seconds per `.py`/`.pyi` file, instead of a fixed 2 minutes. If black does run out of time, the error now states the deadline instead of a bare "signal: killed".
- **Checks run:** `go vet` and `go test ./pkg/formatter` pass locally. I did not run the full gates myself this time: my last full-gates build lost its runner too, so the manager's build is the real test.
- **Backports:** the pull requests to release/2.0–2.6 (#920–#926) are open, each naming the patch tag to cut once it merges. No tag is cut from main, because main is already the 2.7 line.
- **Traces:** this change touches no service handlers, so the trace rule doesn't apply.

The next run acts on the verdict. If the land merges, it writes the outcome comment and closes the issue. If a named gate fails, it fixes that and lands again. If the build infrastructure fails again, it re-lands unchanged.
